Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA
bundle. q2-bandcamp runs from the card's .bandcamp folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's
patch/addon.c): Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page, keeps the Q2
awake while it downloads and plays its URL queues. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.bandcamp, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-bandcamp-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP (from
               q2-filebrowser)
  launcher.sh  installed as .bandcamp/run: q2-bandcamp copied to /tmp and run there at nice 10 in
               a restart loop; it notes its starts and restarts in the debug log, and the app's
               stderr (a crash's message) goes to /tmp/q2-bandcamp.err, which the next start copies
               into the log
  q2app        installed as .bandcamp/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Bandcamp, search=Search
               Bandcamp, qr=0: no phone page)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               installed beside it: Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod), a white
               mark on Bandcamp's blue
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat,
static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries and the firmware's -mfp64 doesn't matter. HTTPS is
checked against Mozilla's CA bundle, which the app carries (internal/tlsroots). On a Q2 whose clock
was never set, certificates are checked at the time a plain-HTTP Date header gives.

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.bandcamp/run when Streaming's Bandcamp row is pressed and it isn't
running. The launcher copies q2-bandcamp and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once, so USB
storage can always take the card. The loop restarts it after a failure, waiting 5 s and doubling to
a minute, and leaves its pid in /tmp/q2-bandcamp. An exit of 0 (Stop Bandcamp, or idle: nothing to
download, the page unused 15 minutes and the proxy unused 30) ends the loop. A TERM to it stops
q2-bandcamp cleanly, the song downloading kept in .bandcamp/partial to resume; an app still there
15 s after it is killed. Q2 Pod sends it for Stop Streaming Services, Home's Rockbox row, an Apps
update or remove, and USB storage (after which it starts it again).

  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.state
      hold (1: a song is downloading), version
  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.sock
      datagrams: q quits
  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page, below
  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.art/<key>.jpg
      the rows' covers ("art" cap): Bandcamp's 100 px pictures, fetched once into img/ and linked
      under each row's key (FNV-1a 32 of its uri, a tab and its context); removed at exit
  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.play, /tmp/q2-bandcamp.urls, /tmp/q2-bandcamp.lyrics/<n>.lrc
      a queue to play ("urls" cap, q2-pod's patch/tidal.c): .play is "<seq> /tmp/q2-bandcamp.urls";
      .urls is "#Q2URLS/1<TAB>start=<i>", then a line a song: its URL (or card path, for a song on
      the card), title, artist, album, cover URL and seconds; a song's lyrics in .lyrics/<n>.lrc
  /tmp/q2-bandcamp.library
      "<seq>\nscan\n": Update Local Music asked for ("library" cap), when the queue empties after
      new songs; Q2 Pod runs it once nothing plays
  127.0.0.1:8117 (the next free one if taken)
      the stream proxy, on the loopback only: /t/<kind>/<list>/<track>.mp3 a song (kind album,
      track, playlist or radio: where it was listed, so its stream address can be asked for again),
      /b/<show>.mp3 a radio show's broadcast, /i/<a|i><id>.jpg a cover (700 px). Range requests
      pass through; a stream address is kept 12 hours and asked for again when Bandcamp refuses it

On the card:

  .bandcamp/queue.json   the jobs waiting, the first one under way
  .bandcamp/done.json    the jobs finished: their folder, songs done, failed and not streamed
  .bandcamp/partial/<track id>.mp3
                         a song being downloaded, in 512 KB chunks, each opened, written, synced and
                         closed (the card is almost never busy); resumed with an HTTP Range; a file
                         untouched for 3 days is removed at a start
  Bandcamp/...           the music (README.md, Where the music goes)
  q2-bandcamp.log        the debug log (q2-bandcamp.old.log: the one before), 512 KB each

The page
--------

Each row's kind says what a press does (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): list opens a level, action sends an
op and toasts its reply, search opens the Q2's keyboard (op search), local plays from the card (a
folder, "/" last, lists its songs; context album: in track order), page moves a long list to its
previous or next page ("window" cap; without it, the reply's cursor and More…), progress draws a
bar of its position (permille), info does nothing. A row's position is the op Play/Pause held sends,
with its context. A reply whose message is "refresh" is asked again every 2 s while on screen: a
list showing a download under way, the menu while downloads wait, Downloads always. A page is 48
rows past its Previous and Next rows.

  menu                       New and Notable, Album of the Day, Playlists, Bandcamp Radio, Search
                             Bandcamp, Downloads, On the Card, Stop Bandcamp
  nn [cursor], aotd [cursor] top10 nn|aotd, then the 120 latest releases
  get <page>                 a release downloaded (a press on its row); a failed one again
  play <page>                a release played (Play/Pause held on its row)
  playlists, fan <id>        playlists; a row opens playlist <id>
  playlist <id> [cursor]     playfrom playlist:<id>:0, getlist playlist:<id> (or its folder and
                             Download Again), then its songs: playfrom, held getalbum
  radio                      Latest Shows (series "") and each series (series <name>)
  series <name> [cursor]     its shows, the newest first: show <id>
  show <id> [cursor]         its blurb, playshow <id>, playfrom radio:<id>:0, getlist radio:<id>,
                             its songs with their minute
  search <text>              releases (get, held play), artists and labels (artist <url>), fans (fan
                             <id>)
  artist <url> [cursor]      getall <url>, then their releases
  downloads [cursor]         the bar of the one under way and cancel <key>, the waiting (cancel),
                             cancelall, the finished (local rows; failures: retry <key>), forget
  card [cursor]              every finished job still on the card, the newest first
  stop                       the reply, then the app stops

Keys: a release's is album:<host><path> (its page, so one album from any list is one), a playlist's
playlist:<id>, a show's radio:<id>. Paths stay under 240 bytes, inside Q2 Pod's 256-byte path buffer
(songs_open): an artist's folder is at most 50 bytes, an album's 70, a song's 80, with the
characters FAT refuses replaced by "_".
